{
  "_": [
    "The temple's catalogue: what it buys, what it keeps on the shelf, and what it pays.",
    "",
    "Every food name here is a name Rajeev's curated recipes actually use, so that when phase 02",
    "imports those recipes the ingredient already exists and is reused instead of created again.",
    "Where the recipes name one thing two ways, the second way is an alias rather than a second",
    "ingredient - the application matches on aliases as well as names, so 'Sabudana' finds Sago.",
    "",
    "Prices are rupees per ONE CANONICAL UNIT (the 'unit' field), Bengaluru wholesale, and are what",
    "a temple buying in bulk would pay. 'opening' is what is on the shelf on the first morning.",
    "",
    "ekadashi: true marks what a Vaishnava does not eat on Ekadashi - grains and pulses. Note what",
    "is deliberately NOT marked: sago, potato, sweet potato, groundnut, milk, ghee, fruit and rock",
    "salt are all eaten on Ekadashi, which is exactly why the temple's Ekadashi dishes are made of",
    "them.",
    "",
    "supply: true is a thing that is bought but never cooked. The application refuses to put one on",
    "a recipe line (KMS-400127), so the two lists are kept apart here too."
  ],
